Package: misscox
Type: Package
Title: Simulation of Missing Covariate Data in Cox Prognostic Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("fossil contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "noreply@github.com")
Description: Rebuilds the simulation study of Marshall, Altman, Royston and Holder
    (2010) <doi:10.1186/1471-2288-10-7>, which compares complete case analysis,
    single imputation and multiple imputation for missing covariates in Cox
    proportional hazards prognostic models. Generates covariates and survival
    times resembling the German Breast Cancer Study Group 2 data, imposes MCAR,
    MAR, MNAR or combined multivariate missingness on four covariates, handles
    the missing data with nine methods (CC, SI, NORM, MIX, MICE, MICE-PMM and
    aregImpute variants) and pools the Cox model results with Rubin's rules.
